    "body": "Was this restriction in Chromium introduced in https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40083787 ?\n\nIf the security issue is relevant then I suppose it should be specified and implemented in other browsers. A bypass shouldn't be in the `sandbox` attribute since it's controlled by the attacker. Maybe instead some opt-in on the \"victim\" side, similar to https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12444 ?",
